        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0453" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/799.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Zamor brothers, Charles and Oreste, are apparently in control of the
                    revolutionary situation, having defeated Davilmar Theodore in battle at Gonaives
                    on February 1. Oreste Zamor has sent a committee of eight to Port au Prince to
                    gain permission of local authorities to enter the city. The reply is likely to
                    be favorable. Zamor plans to establish provisional government and await action
                    of Assembly. He may attempt to dissolve the present Assembly and elect a new
                    one.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
